      {
        "title": {
          "en": "SLAM Watermarking Scheme Preserves LLM Output Quality",
          "zh": "SLAM水印方案保障大型语言模型输出质量"
        },
        "tl_dr": {
          "en": "Researchers introduced SLAM, a new white-box watermarking scheme that embeds marks into the structural geometry of large language models' residual streams to avoid compromising text quality.",
          "zh": "研究人员推出了SLAM，一种新型白盒水印方案，通过将水印嵌入到大型语言模型残差流的结构几何中，从而避免损害文本质量。"
        },
        "key_takeaways": {
          "en": [
            "SLAM is a novel white-box watermarking scheme for large language models.",
            "It avoids compromising text quality, unlike most existing schemes that bias next-token distribution and incur measurable quality loss.",
            "The mark is embedded into the structural geometry of the residual stream, identified by sparse autoencoders encoding linguistic properties."
          ],
          "zh": [
            "SLAM是一种针对大型语言模型的新颖白盒水印方案。",
            "与大多数通过偏置下一词元分布导致可测量质量损失的现有方案不同，SLAM避免了损害文本质量。",
            "水印被嵌入到残差流的结构几何中，通过识别编码语言属性的稀疏自编码器实现。"
          ]
        },
        "impact": {
          "en": "This development is significant for the AI industry as it addresses a key challenge in LLM watermarking: the trade-off between mark detectability and text quality. By preserving output quality, SLAM could facilitate more widespread and trustworthy deployment of LLMs, particularly for applications requiring content provenance without performance degradation.",
          "zh": "这一进展对人工智能行业具有重要意义，因为它解决了大型语言模型水印中的一个关键挑战：水印可检测性与文本质量之间的权衡。通过保持输出质量，SLAM有望促进大型语言模型更广泛、更可靠的部署，特别是对于需要内容溯源而又不影响性能的应用。"
        },
        "source": "arXiv CS.CL",
        "link": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.05443"
      }
    ],
